-12. `tariff.xml` holds tariff versions; a version is in force on every date from its `valid_from` to its `valid_to`, both included, and its bands give a `cents_per_kwh` for each time of day. A depot pays for the energy of a slot the price that its meter applies to that slot under the version in force on the plan date. Each depot's meter has its own way of applying a tariff, the same on every day: it is the one under which every row of `settlements.csv` for that depot is billed exactly its `cents` by the version in force on the row's `settled_date`, and the settlements allow exactly one. A settled session took its `kwh` in equal parts in each slot from `start` to `end`. The energy cost of a plan is the sum over all charges of the depot's price times kWh, in whole cents.
-13. `published_plan.csv` holds the plan published before the disruptions. Only rows whose `plan_date` equals the plan date are read. A row whose `slot_start` is not in its bus's window is rejected as `published_row_outside_window`. A bus's published kWh in a slot is the sum of its accepted rows for that slot.
+12. `tariff.xml` holds tariff versions; a version is in force on every date from its `valid_from` to its `valid_to`, both included, and its bands give a `cents_per_kwh` for each time of day. A depot pays for the energy of a slot the price that its meter applies to that slot under the version in force on the plan date. Each depot's meter reads the tariff as if its clock were shifted by a whole number of slots: for one whole number k from 0 to 95, the same on every day, it applies to the slot that starts at time t the price the bands give the time k times `slot_minutes` minutes after t, wrapping past midnight. A depot's k is the one under which every row of `settlements.csv` for that depot is billed exactly its `cents` by the version in force on the row's `settled_date`; the settlements fit exactly one k per depot. A settled session took its `kwh` in equal parts in each slot from `start` to `end`. The energy cost of a plan is the sum over all charges of the depot's price times kWh, in whole cents.
+13. `published_plan.csv` holds the plan published before the disruptions. Only rows whose `plan_date` equals the plan date are read. A row whose `bus_id` is not a bus on the plan is ignored and is not rejected. A row whose `slot_start` is not in its bus's window is rejected as `published_row_outside_window`. A bus's published kWh in a slot is the sum of its accepted rows for that slot.
